Subject: ui: render graph text with the Noto Sans CJK JP font

The upstream container build replaces DejaVu Sans with Noto Sans CJK JP so
graphs can draw Japanese, Chinese and Korean labels. This patch makes the same
two-file edit to the release tarball the DHI package builds from, so rendered
graphs match the upstream image.

Origin: DHI-internal (reproduces the zabbix-docker build-base font substitution)
Base-Tree: tarball https://cdn.zabbix.com/zabbix/sources/stable/6.0/zabbix-6.0.49.tar.gz sha256:0222e88a8a2c44a99a986bc6cb795133a332d54ba8c327b2bc6494a17d161f6b path=zabbix-6.0.49
Verify: cmd `go test ./package/main/zabbix-web-nginx-pgsql/tests -run TestUIFontPatch -count=1` expect "ok"
Forwarded: not-needed (container packaging choice that zabbix-docker applies at image build time)
Drop-When: never: the release tarball keeps DejaVu Sans and upstream applies this edit only in its image build

--- a/ui/include/defines.inc.php
+++ b/ui/include/defines.inc.php
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@
 define('ELASTICSEARCH_RESPONSE_DOCUMENTS',		2);
 
 define('ZBX_FONTPATH',				realpath('assets/fonts')); // where to search for font (GD > 2.0.18)
-define('ZBX_GRAPH_FONT_NAME',		'DejaVuSans'); // font file name
+define('ZBX_GRAPH_FONT_NAME',		'NotoSansCJKjp-Regular'); // font file name
 define('ZBX_GRAPH_LEGEND_HEIGHT',	120); // when graph height is less then this value, some legend will not show up
 
 define('GRAPH_YAXIS_SIDE_DEFAULT', 0); // 0 - LEFT SIDE, 1 - RIGHT SIDE
@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@
 define('TRIGGERS_OPTION_ALL',				2);
